  "body": "https://github.com/grigio/docker-nixuser/blob/52d7c6de153f05315ac739c1f9b33b829c956040/flake.nix#L64\n\nThe recursive:\n   chmod -R 1000:1000 /nix\n   chmod -R 755 /nix\n\nLeads to a slow docker startup, and additional duplication, as copies the layer (even if the uid and gid match to begin with).\n\nChanging this to:\n   chmod 1000:1000 /nix\n   chmod 755 /nix\n\nAnd setting, so recursive chmod isn't required:\n    pkgs.dockerTools.buildLayeredImage {\n         uid = 1000;\n         gid = 1000;\n    ...\n\nAppears to help.\n\nTiming check via (slow on initial call, faster on subsequent calls):\n```\n  time docker run --rm --entrypoint sh ${IMAGE_NAME} -c 'echo container-started'\n  time docker run --rm ${IMAGE_NAME}\n  \n  docker inspect ${IMAGE_NAME} --format='Entrypoint={{json .Config.Entrypoint}} Cmd={{json .Config.Cmd}}'\n  \n  time /bin/entrypoint\n```\n",
